+
+Versioned memory policy: the evaluator applies a Linux `RLIMIT_AS` soft and
+hard limit before starting `solution.py`. A stricter inherited limit remains
+in effect. Virtual address space includes mappings and interpreter/library
+reservations; it is not measured resident memory (RSS). Descendants inherit
+the per-process limit, but this policy does not enforce a combined process-tree
+budget. An allocation refused by the operating system may be handled by the
+solution; valid output from a process that stays within the limit remains
+eligible for its normal score. Unhandled allocation failures receive the
+existing runtime-error result. The tester and evaluator have separate resource
+budgets. This clarifies and changes the original unspecified memory-accounting
+convention; scores from this version must remain separately identified.
 
